  "text": "Title: Holy Water (Esquire)\nUnder the whirling vortex of the Milky Way, billions and billions of tiny enzyme \nbombs blew up against our ship. We blasted back with a volley of photon torpedoes--\nshoom! shoom!--that wriggled away at hyperwarp speed. Or so it looked from the deck of \nthe electric boat silently carrying us out into Bioluminescent Bay. No doubt it was the \nconflict between the locals and the U. S. Navy here on Vieques that made me see explosions \nin the luminous suds of the boat's wake, and torpedoes in the spooked fish that shot away \nin eerie blue-green streaks.",
